WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.090
On Good Friday, in many Catholic churches,

2
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:08.150
people move slowly around the walls,
stopping at fourteen pictures.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.270
Each picture shows a step on
Jesus' journey to his death.

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.040
People walk from one to
the next and pray at each.

5
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.010
Elsewhere, a woman counts
beads: ten Hail Marys,

6
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.030
again and again.

7
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.870
Why would Catholics stop
at fourteen pictures,

8
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.820
or say the same prayer fifty times?

9
00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.290
In this mission, you'll trace
the Rosary bead by bead,

10
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.450
and its Sorrowful Mysteries.

11
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.120
Then you'll weigh up how much
devotions like these really matter.

12
00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.700
Your mission: explain why
Catholics pray with beads,

13
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.550
pictures and footsteps.
